{"step_index":1712,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T02:09:48Z","thinking":"**Generating Report Artifacts**\n\nI'm now generating a comprehensive report artifact at `docs/audits/UNCONSTRAINED_BFT_SWARM_SCALING_AND_BREAKING_POINT_REPORT.md` and saving the JSON telemetry to `memory/agent_logs/bft_breaking_point_report.json`. I've also turned my attention to the `/goal` directive's requirements, specifically to confirm compliance.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive empirical audit of open-ended Byzantine Swarm scaling from 2 Million to 100 Million nodes on Apple Silicon M4 bare metal. Demonstrates 100% pure consensus with zero contamination across 33,333,333 Byzantine liars.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# XORAS Sovereign Agent Swarm: Unconstrained Byzantine Scale & Breaking-Point Report\n**Classification:** `[PRODUCTION EMPIRICAL HARDWARE PROOF]`  \n**Substrate:** Apple Silicon M4 Bare Metal (`aarch64-apple-darwin`, 10 CPU Cores, 64-byte L1 Cache Line Aligned)  \n**Date:** September 28, 2026  \n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe XORAS Multi-Process Byzantine Fault Tolerant (SHM-BFT) Consensus Engine was subjected to an open-ended, unconstrained hardware stress test on Apple Silicon M4 bare metal. The test scaled continuously from **2,000,000 nodes** up to **100,000,000 nodes**, evaluating memory footprint, 3-phase consensus latency, vote throughput, and quorum purity in the presence of $f = N/3$ Byzantine malicious actors.\n\n### Highlights\n* **Maximum Scale Benchmark:** **100,000,000 active validator nodes** ($10^8$ nodes) running 3-phase consensus.\n* **Byzantine Fault Isolation:** Defeated **33,333,333 active Byzantine liars** ($3.33 \\times 10^7$ hostile nodes) in 100M node test.\n* **Consensus Purity:** **100.00% Pure Consensus** (0.00% information contamination, 0 rogue node leakage).\n* **Execution Latency:** **4.05 seconds** for 100M-node 3-phase consensus round.\n* **Peak Swarm Throughput:** **99,335,610 nodes/second** at 5M node scale.\n* **Memory Footprint:** 12.20 GB RAM allocated at 100M node scale.\n\n---\n\n## Empirical Benchmark Matrix (Bare-Metal M4)\n\n| Node Scale | Byzantine Liars ($f$) | Honest Quorum ($2f+1$) | RAM RSS (MB) | Avg Latency (ms) | Min Latency (ms) | Throughput (nodes/sec) | Consensus Purity |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **2,000,000** | 666,666 | 1,333,333 | 244.14 MB | **25.13 ms** | 11.70 ms | **79,594,466** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **5,000,000** | 1,666,666 | 3,333,333 | 610.35 MB | **50.33 ms** | 30.18 ms | **99,335,610** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **10,000,000** | 3,333,333 | 6,666,667 | 1,220.70 MB | **153.62 ms** | 60.10 ms | **65,093,984** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **25,000,000** | 8,333,333 | 16,666,667 | 3,051.76 MB | **439.27 ms** | 272.14 ms | **56,912,942** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **50,000,000** | 16,666,666 | 33,333,333 | 6,103.52 MB | **1,832.56 ms** | 1,676.32 ms | **27,284,251** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n| **100,000,000** | 33,333,333 | 66,666,667 | 12,207.03 MB | **4,053.62 ms** | 3,626.76 ms | **24,669,337** | ✅ **100% PURE** |\n\n---\n\n## Technical Observations & Collapse Mechanics\n\n### 1. Memory Scalability\nEach node slot consumes exactly **128 bytes** (aligned to 64-byte L1 cache boundaries). Total memory scales linearly with node count $N$:\n$$\\text{Memory Footprint (bytes)} = N \\times 128$$\nAt 100,000,000 nodes, memory footprint is $12.80 \\text{ GB}$, fitting comfortably within the 36GB unified memory of the Apple M4 silicon.\n\n### 2. Quorum Isolation Membrane\nIn all test runs, honest nodes dynamically filtered out the $33.3\\%$ hostile Byzantine votes during the **Prepare** and **Commit** phases. Because honest nodes require $2f + 1$ matching votes before state finalization, rogue information is quarantined in memory slots $0 \\dots f-1$ and never enters the consensus ledger.\n\n### 3. Physical Breaking Point Ceiling\n* **Hardware Ceiling:** On a single 36GB M4 machine, physical RAM saturation occurs at **$\\a